     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen 10,000 mg three times daily is 30 g/day. That is a toxic dose with no therapeutic use, and it risks acute liver failure and death. Normal kidney and liver function and a weight of 70 kg don't change that. A single 10 g dose is already above the usual threshold for serious hepatotoxicity (about 150 mg/kg, or 10.5 g for this patient).\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- 1,000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day)\n- 650 mg PO every 6 hours (2.6 g/day)\n- 1,000 mg PO every 6 hours (4 g/day, the maximum)\n\nIf you're dealing with an acetaminophen overdose, the treatment is N-acetylcysteine with a level-guided workup and poison control (1-800-222-1222), not more acetaminophen. If something else is going on, such as a unit or entry error, tell me the intended dose and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
